# Keep these files byte-for-byte as committed (LF), whatever `core.autocrlf` says.
# GitHub's Windows runners check out with autocrlf on, so without this a Windows
# build sees CRLF copies. usnistgov/sageRecon found exactly that: its Windows
# release carried a rewritten copy of a file it states it ships unmodified.

# Vendored Sage. THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md states which files are unmodified, and
# the re-vendor runbook in MAINTENANCE.md diffs this tree against upstream. Both
# need the bytes to match lazear/sage exactly.
vendor/sage/** -text

# Bundled search templates, compiled into the binary with include_str!. Without
# this, the Windows binary would embed CRLF copies and differ from the others.
assets/templates/*.json -text
